		String	AsIs		Print	Off		Include	'Max.Macros'			Include	'driver.equ.src'		Include	'Common.equ.src'		Include	'hw.equ.src'* change the following equate to update the version numbercurrent_version	equ	$3000		; version is 3.00dev_chars	equ	%0000101111101100 ;device characteristics		Print	On*******************************************************************               Copyright (c) 1988*               Apple Computer, Inc.*               All rights reserved.********************************************************************               UniDisk 3.5 Driver Version 0.10a01** NOTE:         This driver must be installed on the boot*               volume in the subdirectory "/SYSTEM/DRIVERS'.*               Additionally, the FileType for the driver file*               must be set to $00BB.  AuxType is also critical*               to the operating system recognizing the driver*               as a GS/OS device driver.  The AuxType is a long*               word which must have the upper word set to $0000.*               The most significant byte of the least significant*               word in the AuxType must be set to $01 to indicate*               an active GS/OS device driver or $81 to indicate*               an inactive GS/OS device driver.  The least*               significant byte of the least significant word*               of the AuxType field indicates the number of*               devices supported by the driver file.  This value*               should be analogous to the number of DIB's*               contained in the driver file.  GS/OS will only*               install the number of devices indicated in the*               AuxType field.**               GS/OS Device Driver:    FileType = $00BB*                                       AuxType  = $000001XX where:*                                                  XX = number of devices.**               An AuxType of $00000104 indicates four devices.  When*               building a device driver, the best way to set the*               FileType and AuxType is to use the Exerciser to get*               the current file info (GET_FILE_INFO), modify the*               FileType & AuxType and then SET_FILE_INFO.******************************************************************** REVISION HISTORY:** Date_____ Version By_ Description______________________________** 28-Jun-88 0.10a01 RBM Started initial coding.** 06-Jul-88 0.10a02 RBM Added offset to bank $00 parameters to*                       avoid collision with data resulting from*                       calls to the generated driver core routines.** 13-Jul-88 0.10a03 RBM Offline error is no longer lost during a*                       read or write call.** 20-Jul-88 0.12a03 RBM External access bit is now reset after*                       detecting external access.** 03-Aug-88 0.16b01 GRT added get format option!!!!! It was missing.** 09-Aug-88 0.16b01 FAB forced generated driver to remove downloaded unidisk3.5*                       code on driver shutdown.  Patched unidisk3.5/shutdown*                       subroutine called shutdn** 09-Aug-88 0.16b01 FAB added error code when slot arbitor can't give us*                          slot 5 (error= drvr_io_error).  Added in*                          unidisk/startup in subroutine called startup** 13-Aug-88 0.18b02 RBM Detection of external access now updates switch*                       history in DIB.**  9 Mar 89 5.00a13 RBM	Make driver restartable from memory.**  7 Apr 89 5.00d18 RBM Ported generated driver startup and shutdown*			tasks to the loaded driver.  Startup call downloads*			and executes disk switch support code.  Shutdown*			resets the internal hooks, effectively removing the*			disk switch support patch.**  3 May 89 5.00d20 RBM	Fixed missing disk switch on status call $0000.  Both*			insertion and ejection are properly reported now.**  4 Jan 90 6.00d05 GAB Fix for BRC #57779.  In shutdn, the code that restores*			the various parameter lists to their "just-loaded" state*			was not handling the parameter lists for executesw,*			execute_res, and downloadsw.  This has been corrected.*			In addition, the original code was only copying*			every other byte of the image (due to using an*			8-bit accumulator, but decrementing the index*			twice per iteration).  This has been corrected also.**  4 Sep 90 6.00d16 GAB	Fix for the above fix (4 Jan 90).  One byte was left*			off the end of the download parameter block that's*			used to restore the real parameter block at shutdown*			time.  The byte count used to initialize the X-register*			for the restoration loop has been corrected to account*			for this extra byte.** 15 Jan 91 6.00d23 GAB	The driver was incorrectly reporting a disk-switched*			condition during a status call after a successful media*			access call.  This happened because the dsw_history was*			not being updated after the media access call, thereby*			making the status call believe that the last driver call*			had returned an offline error.  The problem has been*			corrected by adding post-processing logic to the read,*			write, and format calls which set up the history correctly*			depending on the results of the call.**			The procedure do_execute and its associated data have*			been removed, since none of it was being used anyways.**			The dispatch procedure has been made slightly more*			efficient by using a JSR (adr,x) addressing mode.**			The Read and Write procedures have been combined into*			a single procedure, since they both do the exact same*			thing anyways.  (They both rely on the generated core*			routines to perform the actual media access.)**			The Open, Close, and Flush routines have been combined*			into a single procedure, since none of them actually*			do anything anyways.  (These functions are only supported*			by character devices.)** 14 Apr 91 6.00d32 GAB Cleared fixed_name bit in device characteristics.** 16 Nov 91         JOA Begin conversion to support mustang ** 20 Nov 91 6.0d59  GAB	Fix bug in Startup call.  When the first call to*			startup discovered that there were no UniDisks*			connected to the system, it left 'the_slot' set*			to -1.  On the second call to startup (for the*			second DIB), the code was checking 'the_slot'*			and assuming that it contained a valid slot*			number. It then made a SmartPort call to the*			indicated slot.  A slot number of -1 translates*			into a physical slot location of $C7xx.  If*			there was no SmartPort in slot 7, the system*			crashed when the call was made.  Fixed by*			checking for a negative 'the_slot' and exiting*			immediately if true (which means that we've*			already scanned all the slots and haven't*			found any more Uni's).**			Removed John's limitation about having multiple*			drives connected to multiple interfaces.******************************************************************		;------------------------------------------;; Equates from procedure ;;------------------------------------------tool_locator 	equ	$E10000		; Tool locator entry pointmac_flag	equ	$0F51		;Mac block read/write flagbuf1		equ	$0C00		;Three work buffers for data off diskbuf2		equ	$0D00		;buf3		equ	$0E00		;cmdbuffl	equ	$42		;parameter variable area (buffer ptr)rtl_addr	equ	$C59C		;rtl instruction in bank $FFread_data	equ	$FF6244		;disk 3.5 driver read data routinetry_more	equ	$FF59C7		;read retry code in romsbset		equ	$FF5A1C		;return point back into rom coderd_hook		equ	$E10F77		;Read data hook routinevector_hook	equ	$E10FA7		;main firmware dispatcherjmp_inst	equ	$5C		;jump long instructioncmdid		equ	$00005A		; firmware internal unitid1		equ	$E10F20		; internal internal unit for drive #1id2		equ	$E10F21		; internal internal unit for drive #2dib_hw_unit	equ	$004A		; (w)  Hardware reference unitg_dispatch	equ	$01FC84		; call generated driver coresp_char		equ	$00C0		; SmartPort DIB characterisicssp_size		equ	sp_char+1	; SmartPort DIB device sizesp_id_len	equ	sp_size+3	; SmartPort DIB id string lengthsp_id_str	equ	sp_id_len+1	; SmartPort DIB id stringsp_type		equ	sp_id_str+16	; SmartPort DIB device typesp_subtype	equ	sp_type+1	; SmartPort DIB device subtypesp_version	equ	sp_subtype+2	; SmartPort DIB versionsp_byte		equ	$00C0		; Undefined   or Error1sp_soft_err	equ	sp_byte+1	; Soft error  or Error2sp_retries	equ	sp_soft_err+1	; Retry count or Error3sp_a_reg	equ	sp_retries+1	; A Register  or Error4sp_x_reg	equ	sp_a_reg+1	; X Register  or Error5sp_y_reg	equ	sp_x_reg+1	; Y Register  or Error6sp_p_reg	equ	sp_y_reg+1	; P Register  or Error7sp_last_byte	equ	sp_p_reg+1	; Undefined   or Error8sp_addr_cnt	equ	$00C0		; SmartPort count word = $0002sp_addr		equ	sp_addr_cnt+2	; SmartPort address for downloadsp_dnld_cnt	equ	$00C0		; SmartPort count word = $xxxxsp_routine	equ	sp_dnld_cnt+2	; SmartPort routine to downloaderror7		equ	$005Cdsw_history	equ	$004C		; (w)  Disk switched historyswitched_bit	equ	%0000000000000001online_bit	equ	%0000000000010000b0_buff_addr	equ	$0052		; (lw) Pointer to bank $00 bufferdsw_current	equ	$004E		; (w)  Current disk switch statusget_sys_buff	equ	$01FC8C		; return address of bank $00 buffer		eject******************************************************************* The following table is the header required for all loaded* drivers which consists of the following:**               Word    Offset from start to 1st DIB*               Word    Number of DIBs*               Word    Offset from start to 1st configuration list*               Word    Offset from start to 2nd configuration list*               etc.******************************************************************		EXPORT	driver_data	driver_data	PROC		dc.w	dib_1-driver_data	; offset to 1st DIB		dc.w	4			; number of devices		dc.w	conf1-driver_data	; offset to 1st configuration list		dc.w	conf2-driver_data	; offset to 2nd configuration list		dc.w	conf3-driver_data	; offset to 3rd configuration list		dc.w	conf4-driver_data	; offset to 4th configuration list** The following are the driver configuration parameter lists.*conf1		dc.w	0		; 0 bytes in parameter listdefault1	dc.w	0		; 0 bytes in default listconf2		dc.w	0		; 0 bytes in parameter listdefault2	dc.w	0		; 0 bytes in default listconf3		dc.w	0		; 0 bytes in parameter listdefault3	dc.w	0		; 0 bytes in default listconf4		dc.w	0		; 0 bytes in parameter listdefault4	dc.w	0		; 0 bytes in default list		eject******************************************************************* The following are tables of format options for each device.* The format option tables have the following structure:**               Word    Number of entries in list*               Word    Display count (number of head links)*               Word    Recommended default option*               Word    Option that current online media is formatted with*               Entries 16 bytes per entry in the format list** The twenty byte structure for each entry in the format list* is as follows:**               Word    Media variables reference number*               Word    Link to reference number n.*               Word    Flags / Format environment*               Long    Number of blocks supported by device*               Word    Block size*               Word    Interleave factor*               Long    Number of bytes defined by flag** Bit definition within the flags word is as follows:*  ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___* |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |* | F | E | D | C | B | A | 9 | 8 | 7 | 6 | 5 | 4 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 0 |* |___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |___|__ Format*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |___|__________ Flags*   |___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|__________________ Reserved** Format Bit Definition: 00   Universal format*                        01   Apple Format*                        02   NonApple Format*                        11   Not Valid** Flag Bit Definition:   00   Size is in bytes*                        01   Size is in Kb*                        02   Size is in Mb*                        11   Size is in Gb******************************************************************format_tbl				;               		dc.w	format1		; pointer to format option list #1		dc.w	format1		; pointer to format option list #2		dc.w	format1		; pointer to format option list #3		dc.w	format1		; pointer to format option list #4format1					; 		dc.w	1		; number of entries		dc.w	1		; number of displayed entries		dc.w	1		; recommended option is 1		dc.w	1		; current media formatted w/option 1format1_entry1				; 		dc.w	1		; RefNum		dc.w	0		; LinkRef		dc.w	4		; univeral format / size in kb		dc.l	1600		; block count		dc.w	512		; block size		dc.w	4		; interleave factor		dc.w	800		; media size is 800kb		eject*******************************************************************               Link Pointer*               Entry Pointer*               Device Characteristics*  ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___* |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |* | F | E | D | C | B | A | 9 | 8 | 7 | 6 | 5 | 4 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 0 |* |___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_ RESERVED	(cleared to 0)*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____ RESERVED	(cleared to 0)*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________ REMOVABLE	*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________ FORMAT	*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________ RESERVED	(cleared to 0)*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________________ READ		*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________________ WRITE	*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________________________ BLOCK DEVICE	*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________________________ SPEED GROUP	(lsb)*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________________________________ SPEED GROUP	(msb)*   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________________________________ FIXED NAME	*   |   |   |   |   |_____________________________________________ RESTARTABLE	*   |   |   |   |_________________________________________________ BUSY		(managed by dispatcher)*   |   |   |_____________________________________________________ LINKED	(partitioned)*   |   |_________________________________________________________ GENERATED	*   |_____________________________________________________________ RAM/ROM DEV	**               Block Count*               Device Name*               Slot Number*               Unit Number*               Device ID Number*               Head Device Link*               Forward Device Link*               Extended DIB Pointer*               DIB device number******************************************************************dib_1            		dc.l	dib_2				; link pointer to second DIB		dc.l	dispatch			; entry pointer		dc.w	dev_chars			; characteristics		dc.l	1600				; block count		dc.b	11				; device name (length & 32 bytes ascii)		dc.b	'UNIDISK3.5A                    '			dc.w	5				; slot # (valid only after startup)dib_subtract	dc.w	0				; unit # (valid only after startup)		dc.w	current_version			; version # 2.00		dc.w	3				; device ID # (valid only after startup)		dc.w	0				; head device link		dc.w	0				; forward device link		dc.l	0				; extended DIB pointer		dc.w	0				; dib device number** The following data is an extension to the DIB required by the generated* driver core routines called the GENERATED DRIVER INFORMATION BLOCK (GDIB).*		dc.w	1				; driver class		dc.w	$0001				; SmartPort Type		dc.w	$0000				; SmartPort Subtype		dc.w	$FFFF				; Cache Mask		dc.w	512				; Device Block Size		dc.w	0				; Device Hardware Unit Number		dc.w	0				; disk switched history		dc.w	0				; current disk switched status		eject*******************************************************************               Link Pointer*               Entry Pointer*               Device Characteristics*  ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___* |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |* | F | E | D | C | B | A | 9 | 8 | 7 | 6 | 5 | 4 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 0 |* |___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |___|_ RESERVED*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________ REMOVABLE*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________ FORMAT*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________ RESERVED*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________________ READ*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________________ WRITE*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________________________ BLOCK DEVICE*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |___|_________________________________ SPEED GROUP*   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________________________________ FIXED NAME*   |   |   |   |   |_____________________________________________ RESTARTABLE*   |   |   |   |_________________________________________________ BUSY*   |   |   |_____________________________________________________ LINKED*   |   |_________________________________________________________ GENERATED*   |_____________________________________________________________ RAM/ROM DEV**               Block Count*               Device Name*               Slot Number*               Unit Number*               Device ID Number*               Head Device Link*               Forward Device Link*               Extended DIB Pointer*               DIB device number******************************************************************dib_2            		dc.l	dib_3				; link pointer to second DIB		dc.l	dispatch			; entry pointer		dc.w	dev_chars			; characteristics		dc.l	1600				; block count		dc.b	11				; device name (length & 32 bytes ascii)		dc.b	'UNIDISK3.5B                    '			dc.w	5				; slot # (valid only after startup)		dc.w	0				; unit # (valid only after startup)		dc.w	current_version			; version # 2.00		dc.w	3				; device ID # (valid only after startup)		dc.w	0				; head device link		dc.w	0				; forward device link		dc.l	0				; extended DIB pointer		dc.w	0				; dib device number** The following data is an extension to the DIB required by the generated* driver core routines called the GENERATED DRIVER INFORMATION BLOCK (GDIB).*		dc.w	1				; driver class		dc.w	$0001				; SmartPort Type		dc.w	$0000				; SmartPort Subtype		dc.w	$FFFF				; Cache Mask		dc.w	512				; Device Block Size		dc.w	0				; Device Hardware Unit Number		dc.w	0				; disk switched history		dc.w	0				; current disk switched status		eject*******************************************************************               Link Pointer*               Entry Pointer*               Device Characteristics*  ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___* |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |* | F | E | D | C | B | A | 9 | 8 | 7 | 6 | 5 | 4 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 0 |* |___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |___|_ RESERVED*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________ REMOVABLE*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________ FORMAT*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________ RESERVED*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________________ READ*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________________ WRITE*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________________________ BLOCK DEVICE*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |___|_________________________________ SPEED GROUP*   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________________________________ FIXED NAME*   |   |   |   |   |_____________________________________________ RESTARTABLE*   |   |   |   |_________________________________________________ BUSY*   |   |   |_____________________________________________________ LINKED*   |   |_________________________________________________________ GENERATED*   |_____________________________________________________________ RAM/ROM DEV**               Block Count*               Device Name*               Slot Number*               Unit Number*               Device ID Number*               Head Device Link*               Forward Device Link*               Extended DIB Pointer*               DIB device number******************************************************************dib_3          		dc.l	dib_4				; link pointer to second DIB		dc.l	dispatch			; entry pointer		dc.w	dev_chars			; characteristics		dc.l	1600				; block count		dc.b	11				; device name (length & 32 bytes ascii)		dc.b	'UNIDISK3.5C                    '			dc.w	5				; slot # (valid only after startup)		dc.w	0				; unit # (valid only after startup)		dc.w	current_version			; version # 2.00		dc.w	3				; device ID # (valid only after startup)		dc.w	0				; head device link		dc.w	0				; forward device link		dc.l	0				; extended DIB pointer		dc.w	0				; dib device number** The following data is an extension to the DIB required by the generated* driver core routines called the GENERATED DRIVER INFORMATION BLOCK (GDIB).*		dc.w	1				; driver class		dc.w	$0001				; SmartPort Type		dc.w	$0000				; SmartPort Subtype		dc.w	$FFFF				; Cache Mask		dc.w	512				; Device Block Size		dc.w	0				; Device Hardware Unit Number		dc.w	0				; disk switched history		dc.w	0				; current disk switched status		eject*******************************************************************               Link Pointer*               Entry Pointer*               Device Characteristics*  ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___* |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |* | F | E | D | C | B | A | 9 | 8 | 7 | 6 | 5 | 4 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 0 |* |___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |___|_ RESERVED*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________ REMOVABLE*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________ FORMAT*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________ RESERVED*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________________ READ*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________________ WRITE*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____________________________ BLOCK DEVICE*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |___|_________________________________ SPEED GROUP*   |   |   |   |   |   |_________________________________________ FIXED NAME*   |   |   |   |   |_____________________________________________ RESTARTABLE*   |   |   |   |_________________________________________________ BUSY*   |   |   |_____________________________________________________ LINKED*   |   |_________________________________________________________ GENERATED*   |_____________________________________________________________ RAM/ROM DEV**               Block Count*               Device Name*               Slot Number*               Unit Number*               Device ID Number*               Head Device Link*               Forward Device Link*               Extended DIB Pointer*               DIB device number******************************************************************dib_4		dc.l	0				; link pointer to second DIB		dc.l	dispatch			; entry pointer		dc.w	dev_chars			; characteristics		dc.l	1600				; block count		dc.b	11				; device name (length & 32 bytes ascii)		dc.b	'UNIDISK3.5D                    '			dc.w	5				; slot # (valid only after startup)		dc.w	0				; unit # (valid only after startup)		dc.w	current_version			; version # 2.00		dc.w	3				; device ID # (valid only after startup)		dc.w	0				; head device link		dc.w	0				; forward device link		dc.l	0				; extended DIB pointer		dc.w	0				; dib device number** The following data is an extension to the DIB required by the generated* driver core routines called the GENERATED DRIVER INFORMATION BLOCK (GDIB).*		dc.w	1				; driver class		dc.w	$0001				; SmartPort Type		dc.w	$0000				; SmartPort Subtype		dc.w	$FFFF				; Cache Mask		dc.w	512				; Device Block Size		dc.w	0				; Device Hardware Unit Number		dc.w	0				; disk switched history		dc.w	0				; current disk switched status		eject******************************************************************* The following table is used to dispatch to GS/OS driver* functions.******************************************************************dispatch_table		dc.w	startup		dc.w	open		dc.w	read		dc.w	write		dc.w	close		dc.w	status		dc.w	control		dc.w	flush		dc.w	shutdnstartup_unit	dc.w	0		; startup unitcurrent_unit	dc.w	0		; current unit being accessedstartup_name	dc.b	'A '		; startup with BLOCK1retry_count	dc.w	0		; retry countdevice_count	dc.w	0		; device countaccess_flag	dc.w	0		; bit 0 set if disk switchedSlotsReg	dc.w	0		;copy of slots reg at startupthe_slot	dc.w	0		eject******************************************************************* DRIVER MAIN ENTRY POINT: DISPATCH** This is the main entry point for the device driver.  The* routine validates the call number prior to dispatching to* the requested function.** Call Number:  $0000   Function: Startup*               $0001             Open*               $0002             Read*               $0003             Write*               $0004             Close*               $0005             Status*               $0006             Control*               $0007             Flush*               $0008             Shutdown*               $0009-$FFFF       Reserved** ENTRY: Call via 'JSL'*     [<drvr_dib_ptr] = Points to the DIB for the device being accessed*       <drvr_dev_num = Device number of device being accessed*      <drvr_call_num = Call number*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT:   Direct page = unchanged with the exception of <drvr_tran_cnt*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 0  0   No error occured*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 1  0   Error occured******************************************************************dispatch		longa	on		longi	on		phb			; save environment		phk		plb		cmp	#max_command	; is it a legal command?		bge	illegal_req	; no		tay			; save command #		ldx	#$0000save_parms				; 		lda	<drvr_dev_num,x	; save GS/OS call parameters		pha		lda	<drvr_blk_num,x		pha		inx		inx		cpx	#$000C		; up to but not including DRVR_TRAN_CNT		bne	save_parms		phy		jsr	set_b0_buff	; set direct page for bank 0 access		ldy	#dsw_current	; init current disk switch status		lda	#0		sta	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		pla			; restore command #		asl	a		; make index to dispatch table		tax		jsr	(|dispatch_table,x) ; call the correct procedure		tay			; save error code		ldx	#$000A		; number of words to restorerestore_parms				; 		pla			; restore GS/OS call parameters		sta	<drvr_blk_num,x		pla		sta	<drvr_dev_num,x		dex		dex		bpl	restore_parms		plb		bcs	gen_exit	; force error code 0 if flag cleared		ldy	#no_errorgen_exit				; 		tya			; restore error code		rtl** Received an illegal request.  Return with an error.*illegal_req				; 		plb			; restore environement		lda	#drvr_bad_req	; set error		sec		rtl		eject******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  STARTUP** This routine must prepare the driver to accept all other driver* calls.  The UniDisk3.5 driver must download a code segment to* the UniDisk device in order to support disk switched errors and* detection of device access external to the operating system.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSR'*     [<drvr_dib_ptr] = Points to the DIB for the device being accessed*       <drvr_dev_num = Device number of device being accessed*      <drvr_call_num = Call number*      <drvr_tran_cnt = $00000000*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 0  0   No error occured*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 1  0   Error occured******************************************************************startup		longa	on		longi	on		lda	the_slot		bmi	no_slot			;if already -1, we've already discovered						; that there are no drives connected.		bne	have_one_slot		jsr	setup_disp_list		; update all dispatch lists ONCE only* setup SlotsReg with contents of slots reg ONCE on 1st startup call		sep	#$20			; 8 bit 'm'		longa	off		lda	>sltromsel		; need slot internal/external		sta	SlotsReg		rep	#$20			; 16 bit 'm'		longa	on				lda	#$0005			; request slot 5 internal		sta	the_slot		jsl	dyn_slot_arbiter		bcc	have_one_slot		; if slot 5 was available				lda	#$000D		sta	the_slottry_another	lda	the_slot		jsl	dyn_slot_arbiter		bcs	nother_slot		jsr	is_XSP_slot		;exteneded SmartPort in slot?		beq	have_one_slot		;yes.nother_slot	jsr	next_slot		bpl	try_anotherno_slot		lda	#drvr_io_error		;can't get slot so exit with error		sec		rts** Need to determine if any UniDisk3.5 devices are connected to* the one slot.  Walk chain starting with device #1.*have_one_slot		@unitLoop		inc	|startup_unit		; device that is being checked		lda	|startup_unit		sta	|current_unit		ldy	#slot_num		lda	the_slot		sta	[drvr_dib_ptr],y	;put the slot number in the DIB 				jsr	setup_disp_unit		; update unit in dispatch lists		jsr	get_sp_dib		; get SmartPort DIB		bcc	@10			; if got result for DIB status call		cmp	#drvr_no_dev		;reached the end of the chain?		bne	no_slot			;no, just skip it then		stz	startup_unit		;reset to unit zero for next slot		bra	nother_slot		;no. and try next slot@10		ldy	#sp_type		; is it a UniDisk3.5 device?		lda	[<b0_buff_addr],y		cmp	#$0001		bne	@unitLoop		; no, keep walking until found / err				ldy	#unit_num		; update DIB		lda	|unitn_unit		; need current unit number		and	#$007F		sta	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		ldy	#dib_hw_unit		sta	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		inc	|device_count		; bump startup count (used for shutdown management)		jsr	dnld_disk_sw		; download disk switch patches to drive		jsr	reset_access		; initialize external access flags		lda	#no_error		clcexit_time		rts		eject***********************************************************************	Is_XSP_slot:**	Entry:	m = 1, x = 1*		SlotsReg = sltromsel register**	Exit:	m = 1, x= 1*		EQ if it is*		NE if it aint (either slot is internal or no SP firmware**  Preserves: 	Y	Uses A,X***********************************************************************		longa	on		longi	onIs_XSP_slot:	lda	the_slot		and	#0007		asl	a		;slot * 2		tax		lda	SlotsReg			and	slotreg_bit-2,x	;is this slot set to external?		beq	@notxSlot	;nope. so don't check any further		txa		lsr	a		ora	#$00C0		xba			;A = $Cs00		tax			;X = $Cs00		longa	off		sep	#$20		lda	>1,x				cmp	#$20		;$Cs01 = $20?		bne	@nextSlot	;nope		lda	>3,x		bne	@nextSlot	;$Cs03 != $00		lda	>5,x		cmp	#$03		;$Cs05 = $03?		bne	@nextSlot		lda	>7,x		bne	@nextSlot	;$Cs07 = $00		lda	>$FB,x		;get smartport ID byte		cmp	#$C0		;have extended and additionals?@nextSlot			longa	on		rep	#$20		rts		@notxSlot	txa			;set NE 		rts		slotreg_bit	dc.w	$0002		;slot 1 slotreg ext bit		dc.w	$0004		;slot 2 slotreg ext bit		dc.w	$0000		dc.w	$0010		;slot 4 slotreg ext bit		dc.w	$0020		;slot 5 slotreg ext bit		dc.w	$0040		;slot 6 slotreg ext bit		dc.w	$0080		;slot 7 slotreg ext bit*********************************************************************** Next_Slot:	calculates next slot number**	creates slot scan in the following order:*	5int,5ext,7ext,6ext,4ext,2ext,1ext***********************************************************************Next_Slot:			lda	the_slot		bmi	@10		asl	a		tax		lda	scanordermap-10,x		sta	the_slot@10		rts		scanordermap	dc.w	$D		;5 -> $D		dc.w	-1		dc.w	-1		dc.w	-1		dc.w	-1		;$9 -> -1		dc.w	9		;$A -> $9		dc.w	-1		dc.w	$A		;$C -> $A		dc.w	$F		;$D -> $F		dc.w	$C		;$E -> $C			dc.w	$E		;$F -> $E		eject******************************************************************* This routine prepares all the dispatch lists which may be used* with the bank $00 core dispatch routines so that they reference* the proper bank $00 address space.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0******************************************************************setup_disp_list          		longa	on		longi	on		ldx	<b0_buff_addr		clc				; update DIB status dispatch list		txa		adc	|unitn_plist_ptr		sta	|unitn_plist_ptr		clc		txa		adc	|unitn_slist_ptr		sta	|unitn_slist_ptr		clc				; update error status dispatch list		lda	<b0_buff_addr		adc	|err7_plist_ptr		sta	|err7_plist_ptr		clc		txa		adc	|err7_slist_ptr		sta	|err7_slist_ptr		clc				; update set address dispatch list		txa		adc	|saddr_plist_ptr		sta	|saddr_plist_ptr		clc		txa		adc	|saddr_clist_ptr		sta	|saddr_clist_ptr		clc				; update download dispatch list		txa		adc	|dnld_plist_ptr		sta	|dnld_plist_ptr		clc		txa		adc	|dnld_clist_ptr		sta	|dnld_clist_ptr		clc				; update download disksw dispatch list		txa		adc	|dnsw_plist_ptr		sta	|dnsw_plist_ptr		clc		txa		adc	|dnsw_clist_ptr		sta	|dnsw_clist_ptr		clc				; update execute disksw dispatch list		txa		adc	|exsw_plist_ptr		sta	|exsw_plist_ptr		clc		txa		adc	|exsw_clist_ptr		sta	|exsw_clist_ptr		clc				; update reset device dispatch list		txa		adc	|exr_plist_ptr		sta	|exr_plist_ptr		clc		txa		adc	|exr_clist_ptr		sta	|exr_clist_ptr		rts		eject******************************************************************* This routine prepares all the dispatch lists which may be used* with the bank $00 core dispatch routines so that they reference* the current unit that is to be accessed.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0******************************************************************setup_cur_unit             		longa	on		longi	on		ldy	#unit_num		; set current unit from DIB		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		sta	|current_unitsetup_disp_unit          		longa	on		longi	on		sep	#$20			; 8 bit 'm'		longa	off		lda	|current_unit		; update parameter list unit numbers		sta	|unitn_unit		sta	|err7_unit		sta	|saddr_unit		sta	|dnld_unit		sta	|dnsw_unit		sta	|exsw_unit		sta	|exr_unit		rep	#$20			; 16 bit 'm'		longa	on		rts		eject******************************************************************* This routine issues a call to the UniDisk3.5 device via the* bank $00 core dispatch routines to execute a DIB status call* or status call $00.  The result is returned in the bank $00* buffer.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0******************************************************************get_sp_dib            		longa	on		longi	on		jsr	set_b0_buff		; init bank $00 buffer pointer		ldy	#8			; copy dispatch list to bank $00copy_unitn_stat		lda	|unitn_stat,y		sta	[<b0_buff_addr],y		dey		dey		bpl	copy_unitn_stat		brl	b0_dispatch		eject******************************************************************* This routine issues a call to the UniDisk3.5 device via the* bank $00 core dispatch routines to execute a set address control* call or control call $06.  The address is passed in the bank* $00 buffer.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSR'*               A Reg = Address to set*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0******************************************************************do_set_address           		longa	on		longi	on		jsr	set_b0_buff		; init bank $00 buffer pointer		ldy	#sp_addr		; set download address & count		sta	[<b0_buff_addr],y		dey		dey		lda	#2		sta	[<b0_buff_addr],y		ldy	#8			; copy dispatch list to bank $00copy_set_addr		lda	|set_addr,y		sta	[<b0_buff_addr],y		dey		dey		bpl	copy_set_addr		bra	b0_dispatch		eject******************************************************************* This routine issues a call to the UniDisk3.5 device via the* bank $00 core dispatch routines to execute a download control* call or control call $07.  The download routine is passed in* the bank $00 buffer.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Pointer to Dowload Routine*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0******************************************************************do_download        		longa	on		longi	on		jsr	set_b0_buff		; init bank $00 buffer pointer		ldy	#sp_dnld_cnt		lda	#$0001			; count in control list		sta	[<b0_buff_addr],y		iny		iny		lda	#$0008			; Data to download		sta	[<b0_buff_addr],ycopy_dnld_list		ldy	#8			; copy dispatch list to bank $00copy_download		lda	|download,y		sta	[<b0_buff_addr],y		dey		dey		bpl	copy_download		bra	b0_dispatch		eject******************************************************************* This routine issues a call to the UniDisk3.5 device via the* bank $00 core dispatch routines to execute a download control* call or control call $07.  The download resets all the hooks* internal to the UniDisk3.5 drive.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Pointer to Dowload Routine*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0******************************************************************		EXPORT	do_other_dnlddo_other_dnld           		longa	on		longi	on		jsr	set_b0_buff		; init bank $00 buffer pointer		ldx	#$0000		ldy	#sp_dnld_cnthook_loop		lda	|hook_addr,x		; copy hook table to UniDisk3.5		sta	[<b0_buff_addr],y		iny		iny		inx		inx		cpx	#$0018		bne	hook_loop		bra	copy_dnld_list		eject******************************************************************* This routine issues a call to the UniDisk3.5 device via the* bank $00 core dispatch routines to execute a diagnostic status* call or status call $05.  The result status list is passed in* the bank $00 buffer.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0******************************************************************do_diag_status      		longa	on		longi	on		jsr	set_b0_buff		; init bank $00 buffer pointer		ldy	#8			; copy dispatch list to bank $00copy_err7_stat		lda	|err7_stat,y		sta	[<b0_buff_addr],y		dey		dey		bpl	copy_err7_stat		eject******************************************************************* This routine actually sets up and executes the dispatch to the* bank $00 core dispatch routines.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 0  0 = No error*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 1  0 = Error******************************************************************b0_dispatch    		longa	on		longi	on		ldx	<b0_buff_addr		; setup & execute SmartPort call		pea	<b0_buff_addr+1		plb		plb		lda	<drvr_dev_num		jsl	to_b0_core		; call SmartPort via core dispatcher		phk		plb		bcc	no_b0_error		; if no error from SmartPort		php		pha		cmp	#drvr_disk_sw		; was it a disk switched error?		bne	not_disk_sw		; no		ldy	#dsw_current		; set disk switch flag		lda	#$0001		sta	[<drvr_dib_ptr],ynot_disk_sw		pla		plpno_b0_error		rts		eject******************************************************************* This routine issues a call to the UniDisk3.5 device via the* bank $00 core dispatch routines to execute a download and execute* to install the disk switch patch.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0******************************************************************dnld_disk_sw            		longa	on		longi	on		jsr	set_b0_buff		; init bank $00 buffer pointer				lda	#$0700			; set address for download		jsr	do_set_address				ldy	#78			; copy dispatch list to bank $00copy_dnldsw		lda	|downloadsw,y		sta	[<b0_buff_addr],y		dey		dey		bpl	copy_dnldsw		jsr	b0_dispatch		; issue download call				jsr	set_b0_buff		; init bank $00 buffer pointer		ldy	#16			; copy dispatch list to bank $00copy_exec_sw		lda	|executesw,y		sta	[<b0_buff_addr],y		dey		dey		bpl	copy_exec_sw		brl	b0_dispatch		; issue execute call		eject******************************************************************* This routine issues a call to the UniDisk3.5 device via the* bank $00 core dispatch routines to execute an execute* to remove the disk switch patch.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0******************************************************************delete_patch		longa	on		longi	on		jsr	set_b0_buff		; init bank $00 buffer pointer		ldy	#16			; copy dispatch list to bank $00copy_ex_r		lda	|execute_res,y		sta	[<b0_buff_addr],y		dey		dey		bpl	copy_ex_r		brl	b0_dispatch		; issue execute call		eject******************************************************************* Before returning, set the value of ERROR7 (UniDisk3.5 direct* page location $005C) so that bit 3 is set to indicate that* decimal mode is active.  Any UniDisk call with the exception of* status call $05 (diagnostic status) will clear bit 3 of ERROR7.* This bit will be examined prior to dispatching to the device* in order to detect a direct external access.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Unchanged*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0  Unchanged******************************************************************reset_access       		longa	on		longi	on		php		pha		lda	#$0072			; set address for hook table		jsr	do_set_address		jsr	do_other_dnld		lda	#error7			; set address to ERROR7		jsr	do_set_address		jsr	do_download		pla		plp		rts		eject******************************************************************* This routine is used to detect if decimal mode is indicated* by ERROR7 (UniDisk3.5 zero page location $005C).  If decimal* mode is active then no direct external access has occured.* if decimal mode is not active then direct external access has* occured and will result in a disk switch status or error as* appropriate for the current device call.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 0  0  no external access occurred*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 1  0  external access occured******************************************************************check_access    		longa	on		longi	on		jsr	do_diag_status		; execute status call $05		bcc	have_access		; if no error on status call				lda	#%00000001		; else, assume disk switched		bra	fake_accesshave_access		ldy	#sp_p_reg		; get UniDisk processor status		lda	[<b0_buff_addr],y		eor	#$0008			; inverse of decimal bit indicates switch		and	#$0008		ror	a		ror	a		ror	a			; bit 1 = disk switchfake_access		ldy	#dsw_current		; OR in any diskswitch this drvr call		ora	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		sta	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		ror	a			; c = DiskSwitch		lda	#drvr_disk_sw		; assume an error		rts		eject******************************************************************* This routine is used to set the location B0_BUFF_ADDR to* point to the system buffer in bank $00.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Unchanged*               X Reg = Unchanged*               Y Reg = Unchanged*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Unchanged*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0******************************************************************set_b0_buff         		longa	on		longi	on		php		pha		phx		phy		phb		jsl	get_sys_buff		; return bank $00 buffer in X reg.		clc		txa		adc	#$0100		sta	<b0_buff_addr		stz	<b0_buff_addr+2		plb		ply		plx		pla		plp		rts		eject******************************************************************* The following data area contains images of dispatch lists to* be used for calls to the UniDisk3.5 firmware via the bank $00* core dispatch routine.  Note that these images must be updated* for the bank $00 buffer address and the current unit to be* accessed.  A common update routine is provided for this purpose.* Bank zero buffer usage is as follows:**				 _______________________* 			+$01FX	|			|*			+$01EX	|			|*			+$01DX	|			|*			+$01CX	|_______________________| <- Status / Control list*			+$01BX	|			|*			+$01AX	|			|*			+$019X	|			|*			+$018X	|			|*			+$017X	|			|*			+$016X	|			|*			+$015X	|			|*			+$014X	|			|*			+$013X	|			|*			+$012X	|			|*			+$011X	|			|*	b0_buff_addr	+$010X	|_______________________| <- SmartPort parameter block* 			+$00FX	|			|*			+$00EX	|			|*			+$00DX	|			|*			+$00CX	|			|*			+$00BX	|			|*			+$00AX	|			|*			+$009X	|			|*			+$008X	|	   Do		|*			+$007X	|	   Not		|*			+$006X	|	   Use		|*			+$005X	|			|*			+$004X	|			|*			+$003X	|			|*			+$002X	|			|*			+$001X	|			|*			+$000X	|_______________________| <- This area used by generated core** SmartPort parmater block (as passed to bank 0 core):**				dc.b	command*				dc.w	parameter list pointer*	parameter list pointer	dc.b	parameter count*				dc.b	unit number*				dc.w	pointer to status / control list*				dc.b	status / control code******************************************************************parms_start** The following is the parameter list for a unit N status call* to the SmartPort.  This is used to determine the device type* and subtype.*unitn_stat	dc.b	$00		; status callunitn_plist_ptr	dc.w	$0003		; pointer to parameter listunitn_plist	dc.b	3		; parameter countunitn_unit	dc.b	1		; unit numberunitn_slist_ptr	dc.w	$00C0		; pointer to status list		dc.b	3		; status code = DIB status** The following is the parameter list for a unit N status call* to the SmartPort.  This is used to determine the state of* location ERROR7 ($005C) from the internal zero page resident* within the UniDisk3.5 device.*err7_stat	dc.b	$00		; status callerr7_plist_ptr	dc.w	$0003		; pointer to parameter listerr7_plist	dc.b	3		; parameter counterr7_unit	dc.b	1		; unit numbererr7_slist_ptr	dc.w	$00C0		; pointer to status list		dc.b	5		; status code = diagnostic status** The following is the parameter list for a unit N set download address call.*set_addr	dc.b	$04		; control callsaddr_plist_ptr	dc.w	$0003		; pointer to parameter listsaddr_plist	dc.b	3		; parameter countsaddr_unit	dc.b	1		; unit numbersaddr_clist_ptr	dc.w	$00C0		; pointer to status list		dc.b	6		; control code = set address** The following is the parameter list for a unit N download call.*download	dc.b	$04		; control calldnld_plist_ptr	dc.w	$0003		; pointer to parameter listdnld_plist	dc.b	3		; parameter countdnld_unit	dc.b	1		; unit numberdnld_clist_ptr	dc.w	$00C0		; pointer to status list		dc.b	7		; control code = down loadhook_addr	dc.w	21		jmp	$E106		jmp	$E203		jmp	$EF03		jmp	$E492		jmp	$E2CF		jmp	$E317		jmp	$E464		eject******************************************************************* The following data is actually the object code that is to be* downloaded to UniDisk3.5 devices in order to support the disk* switched status code. This code will be downloaded to* address $0700 within the UniDisk3.5 internal RAM.** NOTE: The count word must always be an even number!!!******************************************************************** The following is the parameter list for a unit N execute call.*executesw	dc.b	$04		; control callexsw_plist_ptr	dc.w	$0003		; pointer to parameter listexsw_plist	dc.b	3		; parameter countexsw_unit	dc.b	1		; unit numberexsw_clist_ptr	dc.w	$0008		; pointer to status list		dc.b	5		; control code = executeexsw_parms	dc.w	6		; count word		dc.b	0		; A register		dc.b	0		; X register		dc.b	0		; Y register		dc.b	%00100100	; N V ¥ÊBÊD I Z C		dc.w	$0700		; Program counter** The following is the parameter list for a unit N execute RESET call.*execute_res	dc.b	$04		; control callexr_plist_ptr	dc.w	$0003		; pointer to parameter listexr_plist	dc.b	3		; parameter countexr_unit	dc.b	1		; unit numberexr_clist_ptr	dc.w	$0008		; pointer to status list		dc.b	5		; control code = executeexr_parms	dc.w	6		; count word		dc.b	0		; A register		dc.b	0		; X register		dc.b	0		; Y register		dc.b	%00100100	; N V ¥ÊBÊD I Z C		dc.w	$E7D9		; Program counter; include the following line to ensure that there are an even # of bytes in; this block of data (the various parameter blocks). 		dc.b	0		;make sure there's an even # of bytes		eject******************************************************************* The following is the parameter list for a unit N download call.******************************************************************downloadsw	dc.b	$04		; control calldnsw_plist_ptr	dc.w	$0003		; pointer to parameter listdnsw_plist	dc.b	3		; parameter countdnsw_unit	dc.b	1		; unit numberdnsw_clist_ptr	dc.w	$0008		; pointer to status list		dc.b	7		; control code = down loadparms_end if (((parms_end-parms_start)//2)<>0) then 	aerror	'Uneven # of bytes in SmartPort parameter lists' endifdisksw_data	dc.w	70		; # bytes to be downloaded					; patch code follows.....******************************************************************* This routine is downloaded to the UniDisk3.5 driver at location $0700.* This routine is installed inline with the main entry point in the* UniDisk3.5 internal firmware and monitors a zero page location executed* during the EJECT process.  The location MIDEJECT within the UniDisk3.5* internal zero page contains values of $01, $02 or $80 as a result of an* eject operation.  Our patch installs a value of $C0 (bit 6 set) to * indicate that an eject has not occured.  Bit 6 of location MIDEJECT will * be cleared if an eject occurs.  The remainder of the patch is installed* in-line with the UniDisk3.5 firmware SmartPort command dispatcher and * monitors the state of bit 6 in location MIDEJECT.  If bit 6 is cleared,* a DISKSW error will be returned and bit 6 will be SET.  Note that the* DISKSW error will only be returned from the UniDisk3.5 on a READBLOCK, * WRITEBLOCK, READBYTES or WRITEBYTES call (SmartPort).  Note that the* location that this patch resides at in the UniDisk3.5 memory map cannot* move and cannot grow beyond the length of 64 bytes.  All other available* free memory in the UniDisk3.5 internal memory map has been made available* to the developer community and cannot be used for compatibility sake.**					; Entry via a 'JSR'*					;	A Reg =	$00*					;	X Reg =	$00*					;	Y Reg =	$00*					;	P Reg =	N V ¥ÊBÊD I Z C*					;		x x x 0 0 x x x*					;	PC    =	$0700*					;*					; Exit via a 'RTS'*					;	A Reg =	$00*					;	X Reg =	$00*					;	Y Reg =	$00*					;	P Reg =	N V ¥ÊBÊD I Z C*					;		x x x 0 0 x x x*					;	PC    =	$0700*					;******************************************************************					;mideject	equ	$006F	; location used by eject code*					;vector_hook	equ	$0087	; main entry vector*					;cmdcode	equ	$004C	; location of SmartPort command*					;statbyte	equ	$005E	; error status returned by SmartPort*					;bytecountl	equ	$003F	; byte count LSB*					;bytecounth	equ	$0040	; byte count MSB*					;*                                       ;init		start		dc.b	$A2,$02		;		ldx	#$02*                                       ;movehook	anop		dc.b	$B5,$87		;		lda	<vector_hook,x	; patch main entry		dc.b	$9D,$3C,$07	;		sta	|execute,x		dc.b	$CA		;		dex		dc.b	$10,$F8		;		bpl	movehook		dc.b	$A9,$17		;		lda	#<swstat		dc.b	$85,$88		;		sta	oldhook+1		dc.b	$A9,$07		;		lda	#>swtat		dc.b	$85,$89		;		sta	oldhook+2*                                       ;init_mid	anop		dc.b	$A9,$C0		;		lda	#notsw		; bit 6 says not switched		dc.b	$85,$6F		;		sta	mideject		dc.b	$60		;		rts*                                       ;*                                       ;swstat		anop		dc.b	$A5,$4C		;		lda	cmdcode		; is it a status call?		dc.b	$F0,$13		;		beq	chk_sw		; yes		dc.b	$C9,$05		;		cmp	#$05		; is it an init call?		dc.b	$D0,$06		;		bne	not_init	; no		dc.b	$20,$D9,$E7	;		jsr	init_hooks	; else restore hooks		dc.b	$4C,$87,$00	;		jmp	vectorhook	; and execute init call*                                       ;not_init	anop		dc.b	$C9,$03		;		cmp	#$03		; is it a rdblk or wrblk?		dc.b	$B0,$01		;		bge	cmd_chk		; no		dc.b	$3A		;		dec			; yes, translate*                                       ;cmd_chk	anop		dc.b	$29,$06		;		and	#%11110110	; is it rdblk, wrblk, rd or wr?		dc.b	$D0,$0E		;		bne	execute		; no		dc.b	$24,$6F		;		bit	mideject	; has eject occured?		dc.b	$70,$0A		;		bvs	execute		; no, execute call		dc.b	$A9,$AE		;		lda	#disksw+$80	; else return disk switch error		dc.b	$85,$5E		;		sta	statbyte		dc.b	$64,$3F		;		stz	bytecountl	; byte count on error is zero		dc.b	$64,$40		;		stz	bytecounth		dc.b	$80,$D6		;		bra	init_mid	; set disk not switched flag*                                       ;execute	anop		dc.b	$4C,$FD,$00	;		jmp	newhook		; execute the call		eject******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  OPEN* DRIVER CALL:  CLOSE* DRIVER CALL:  FLUSH** These calls have no application with block device drivers and will* return with no error.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*      <drvr_tran_cnt = $00000000*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 0  0   No error occured*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 1  0   Error occured******************************************************************opencloseflush		longa	on		longi	on		lda	#no_error		clc		rts		eject******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  READ** This call executes a read from the device.  Block devices must* validate the initial block number and that the request count is* an integral multiple of the block size.  In addition the block* number of each successive block must be validated as it is* accessed when an multiple block I/O transaction is in place.** DRIVER CALL:  WRITE** This call executes a write to the device.  Block devices must* validate the initial block number and that the request count is* an integral multiple of the block size.  In addition the block* number of each successive block must be validated as it is* accessed when an multiple block I/O transaction is in place.** Note that both functions can be handled by this single procedure,* since the procedure simply calls the generated core driver routines* to perform the actual media access.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*       <drvr_buf_ptr = Pointer to I/O buffer*       <drvr_blk_num = Initial block number*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred*      <drvr_blk_size = Size of block to be accessed*      <drvr_tran_cnt = $00000000*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 0  0  if no error*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 1  0  if error******************************************************************readwrite		longa	on		longi	on		lda	<drvr_blk_size		; validate the current block size		cmp	#$0200		beq	do_access		cmp	#$020C		beq	do_access		lda	#drvr_bad_parm		; invalid block size		sec		rtsdo_access		jsr	setup_cur_unit		; adjust unit parameter		jsr	check_access		; did direct access occur?		bcs	almost_done		; yes		jsl	g_dispatch		; pass call on to generated corealmost_done		jsr	reset_access		; prepare for direct access detectionset_history					; entry point used after a format call		bcs	@chk_offline		; if error occured (v0.10a03)		ldy	#dsw_current		; did disk switch occur?		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		bne	@set_switched		; yes, make sure history is updated		ldy	#dsw_history		; update the history		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		and	#Åswitched_bit		; clear the switched bit		ora	#$8000+online_bit	; and set the online bit		sta	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		lda	#no_error		; return no error		rts@set_switched		lda	#$8000+switched_bit	; set switched bit and clear online bit		ldy	#dsw_history		sta	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		lda	#drvr_disk_sw		; else return disk switched error@call_done		cmp	#$0001			; condition carry		rts@chk_offline		cmp	#drvr_off_line		; no disk in drive?		bne	@call_done		; nope, must be sump'in else!		ldy	#dsw_history		; else update our history word		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		and	#Åonline_bit		; clear the online bit in the history		sta	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		lda	#drvr_off_line		; return the offline error		sec		rts		eject******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  STATUS** This routine supports all the standard device status calls.* Any status call which is able to detect an OFFLINE or DISK* SWITCHED condition should call the system service routine* SET_DISKSW.  OFFLINE and DISKSW are conditions and not errors* when detected by a status call and should only be returned as* conditions in the status list.** Status Code:  $0000   Return Device Status*               $0001   Return Control Parameters*               $0002   Return Wait/No Wait Mode*               $0003   Return Format Options** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*     <drvr_clist_ptr = Pointer to control list*     <drvr_ctrl_code = Control code*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred*      <drvr_tran_cnt = $00000000*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 0  0   No error occured*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 1  0   Error occured******************************************************************status		longa	on		longi	on		lda	<drvr_stat_code		;is this a get format option call		cmp	#drvr_get_format		beq	get_format		;yes		stz	|access_flag		; assume no access occurred		jsr	setup_cur_unit		; adjust unit parameter		jsr	check_access		; did direct access occur?		php		rol	|access_flag		; access = disk switch		plp		bcc	ok			; if no direct access occured		jsl	set_disksw		; delete cache & mark VCR'sok						; 		jsl	g_dispatch		; pass call on to generated core		jsr	reset_access		; prepare for direct access detectioncall_done1					; 		bcs	stat_done		; if error, history cant be updated		lda	<drvr_stat_code		; is this a return from device status?		bne	stat_done		; no		eject** On return from a device status call, only the first offline and disk switch* status should be returned while the media remains offline.  Subsequent status* calls with the media offline should return only the offline and omit the* disk switched status.  Prior to checking the history, any direct access* detection is ORed in as a disk switch status.*		ldy	#dsw_current		; was disk switch returned this call		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y	; bit 0 set if disksw error returned (fw)		ora	|access_flag		; bit 0 set if external firmware access		ora	[<drvr_slist_ptr]		sta	[<drvr_slist_ptr]	; status = firmware + access + current		ldy	#dsw_history		; has history ever been set?		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		bpl	update_history		; no, go initialize historycheck_history		eor	[<drvr_slist_ptr]	; offline/online reported before?		and	#$0010		beq	update_history		; yes		lda	#$0001			; no, indicate switch		ora	[<drvr_slist_ptr]		sta	[<drvr_slist_ptr]update_history					; 		lda	[<drvr_slist_ptr]		and	#$0011			; want only offline and disk sw		ora	#$8000			; history must never = $0000		sta	[<drvr_dib_ptr],ystat_done					; 		lda	#no_error		clc		rts		eject******************************************************************* This routine returns the format options for the device.* Consult the driver specification for the format option list.* This call requires a minimum request count of $00000002.  The* maximum request count may exceed the size of the format list* in which case the request count returned will indicate the* size of the format list.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 0  0   No error occured*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 1  0   Error occured******************************************************************get_format					;               		longa	on		longi	on		lda	#drvr_bad_parm		; assume invalid request count		ldx	<drvr_req_cnt+2		; and validate request count		bne	bad_get_format		ldx	<drvr_req_cnt		cpx	#$0002		bge	ok_get_formatbad_get_format					; 		sec		rts** Request count is valid. Return the format options for this device.*ok_get_format					; 		ldy	#dib_hw_unit		; internal device #		sec		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		sbc	>dib_subtract		; convert hardware units to 0 thru 4		asl	a		tax		lda	|format_tbl,x		; get pointer to format option list		tax		lda	|0,x			; get # entries in option list		asl	a			; list length = (n * 16) + 8		asl	a		asl	a		asl	a		clc		adc	#$0008			; now have option list length		cmp	<drvr_req_cnt		; is request longer then list length?		bge	req_count_ok		sta	<drvr_req_cntreq_count_ok					; 		ldy	#$0000			; status list index		sep	#$20			; 8 bit 'm'		longa	offcopy_format					; 		lda	|0,x			; copy format option list to slist_ptr		sta	[<drvr_slist_ptr],y		inx		iny		cpy	<drvr_req_cnt		; copy = request count size		bne	copy_format		rep	#$20			; 16 bit 'm'		longa	on		EXPORT	set_xfer_cntset_xfer_cnt					;               		lda	<drvr_req_cnt		; set transfer count		sta	<drvr_tran_cnt		lda	<drvr_req_cnt+2		sta	<drvr_tran_cnt+2		lda	#no_error		; and return with no error		clc		rts		eject******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  CONTROL** This routine supports all the standard device control calls.** Control Code: $0000   Reset Device*               $0001   Format Device*               $0002   eject Media*               $0003   Set Control Parameters*               $0004   Set Wait/No Wait Mode*               $0005   Set Format Options*               $0006   Assign Partition Owner*               $0007   Arm Signal*               $0008   Disarm Signal** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*     <drvr_clist_ptr = Pointer to control list*     <drvr_ctrl_code = Control code*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred*      <drvr_tran_cnt = $00000000*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 0  0   No error occured*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 1  0   Error occured******************************************************************control		longa	on		longi	on		stz	|access_flag		; assume no access occurred		jsr	setup_cur_unit		; adjust unit parameter		jsr	check_access		; did direct access occur?		bcc	ok1			; if no direct access occured		jsl	set_disksw		; delete cache & mark VCR'sok1						; 		jsl	g_dispatch		; pass call on to generated core		jsr	reset_access		; prepare for direct access detection		ldx	<drvr_ctrl_code		; was this a format call?		dex				; (this doesn't change the carry bit)		beq	@post_process		; yes, must update our history word		rts@post_process	jmp	set_history		; go condition the history word		eject******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  SHUTDOWN** This call prepares the driver for shutdown.  This may include* closing a character device as well as releasing any and all* system resources that may have been aquired by either a* STARTUP or OPEN call.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*      <drvr_tran_cnt = $00000000*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ ¥  0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 0  0   No error occured*                       ¥ ¥ 0 0 0 0 ¥ 1  0   Error occured******************************************************************shutdn		longa	on		longi	on		jsr	setup_cur_unit		; adjust unit parameter		jsr	delete_patch		; remove disk switch patch		dec	|device_count		; number of appledisk3.5's online		bne	not_last		stz	the_slot		;reset slot to unknown; reinitialize all variables (for a possible warm-start)		ldx	#restore_end-restore_tbl-2restore_loop		lda	|restore_tbl,x		sta	|startup_unit,x		dex		dex		bpl	restore_loop				ldx	#restore1_end-restore_1-2		restore1_loop		lda	|restore_1,x		sta	|unitn_stat,x		dex		dex		bpl	restore1_loop				lda	#no_error		; no error if all shutdown		clc		rtsnot_last		lda	#drvr_busy		; else return busy		sec		rtsrestore_tbl	dc.w	0			; startup unit		dc.w	0			; current unit being accessed		dc.b	'A '			; startup with BLOCK1		dc.w	0			; retry count		dc.w	0			; device count		dc.w	0			; bit 0 set if disk switchedrestore_end; the following values are used to restore the various parameter lists to their "just-loaded"; state.  This allows the driver to be restartable from memory (so it doesn't have to be; reloaded when switching from P8 to GS/OS).  The values were copied directly from their; original locations.restore_1; parms for unitn_stat		dc.b	$00			; status call		dc.w	$0003			; pointer to parameter list		dc.b	3			; parameter count		dc.b	1			; unit number		dc.w	$00C0			; pointer to status list		dc.b	3			; status code = DIB status; parms for err7_stat		dc.b	$00			; status call		dc.w	$0003			; pointer to parameter list		dc.b	3			; parameter count		dc.b	1			; unit number		dc.w	$00C0			; pointer to status list		dc.b	5			; status code = diagnostic status; parms for set_addr		dc.b	$04			; control call		dc.w	$0003			; pointer to parameter list		dc.b	3			; parameter count		dc.b	1			; unit number		dc.w	$00C0			; pointer to status list		dc.b	6			; control code = set address; parms for download		dc.b	$04			; control call		dc.w	$0003			; pointer to parameter list		dc.b	3			; parameter count		dc.b	1			; unit number		dc.w	$00C0			; pointer to status list		dc.b	7			; control code = down load; parms for hook_addr		dc.w	21		jmp	$E106		jmp	$E203		jmp	$EF03		jmp	$E492		jmp	$E2CF		jmp	$E317		jmp	$E464; parms for executesw		dc.b	$04		; control call		dc.w	$0003		; pointer to parameter list		dc.b	3		; parameter count		dc.b	1		; unit number		dc.w	$0008		; pointer to status list		dc.b	5		; control code = execute		dc.w	6		; count word		dc.b	0		; A register		dc.b	0		; X register		dc.b	0		; Y register		dc.b	%00100100	; N V ¥ÊBÊD I Z C		dc.w	$0700		; Program counter; parms for execute_res		dc.b	$04		; control call		dc.w	$0003		; pointer to parameter list		dc.b	3		; parameter count		dc.b	1		; unit number		dc.w	$0008		; pointer to status list		dc.b	5		; control code = execute		dc.w	6		; count word		dc.b	0		; A register		dc.b	0		; X register		dc.b	0		; Y register		dc.b	%00100100	; N V ¥ÊBÊD I Z C		dc.w	$E7D9		; Program counter if (((parms_end-parms_start)//2)<>0) then 		dc.b	0		;make sure there's an even # of bytes endif; parms for downloadsw		dc.b	$04		; control call		dc.w	$0003		; pointer to parameter list		dc.b	3		; parameter count		dc.b	1		; unit number		dc.w	$0008		; pointer to status list		dc.b	7		; control code = down loadrestore1_end		endp				end